{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures","id":1448909,"title":"Are Kuei-jin Wyrm creatures?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-18T16:08:27-07:00","id":1448909,"title":"Are Kuei-jin Wyrm creatures?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> As the title says, are Kuei-jin of the Wyrm? Especially for Rites and Gifts purposes, do they count as tainted?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T17:16:01-07:00","id":1448916,"title":"","content":"I would say not inherently---in fact inherently they're creatures of &quot;balance&quot; and potentially somewhat resistant (having both Lifesight and Deathsight, they can shift between lower and middle umbral energies; they're not just undead revenants but creatures of both flesh and spirit, somewhat like Garou). However, those of the Scorpion Eater Dharma, and those who have outright become Akuma, are extremely of-the-Wyrm. From a WTA perspective I'd translate the Yama Kings as essentially corrupted Incarnae of some sort or other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T17:56:16-07:00","id":1448918,"title":"","content":"IIRC it depends on their current chi balance. Balanced and yang imbalanced don't ping as Wyrm. Ying imbalance (because of the death energy), high level of demon chi, and having tainted chi, should all ping as having Wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> They most certainly aren't inherently creatures of the Wyrm, so things like Rite of Cleansing wouldn't just cause them pain. Though letting it manipulate chi levels is probably a bit much for a level 1 Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T18:49:44-07:00","id":1448922,"title":"","content":"They ping by default and get pained by rites of cleansing unless they are very far on particular Dharmas - the books cited the Resplendent Cranes as being more Weaver aligned (more's the pity, also bad) and Thrashing Dragons as Wyld-aligned (to detrimental levels). This generally doesn't kick in until you're at level 7. Alternately, if one had Hun 7, that might also do the trick for not pinging, though for characters right out of chargen, that means giving up the capacity to use Willpower to buy successes. And also 18 freebie points, so you'd need to use merits and flaws to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T18:56:15-07:00","id":1448924,"title":"","content":"I would treat them like vampires. The dead should stay dead, so yes they are Wyrm creatures. But not all of them may detect as the Wyrm just like high humanity vampires don't. There are lots of creatures like that. Wraiths in the Underworld don't detect as Wyrm because that is where they belong, but if they cross over into the living world they do. And Spectres are Wyrm tainted. <br /> <br /> But that's only my head logic, not an official rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T18:58:59-07:00","id":1448925,"title":"","content":"(Reference Note: By canon, wraiths only register to Sense Wyrm if the Shadow's Angst is greater than the Psyche's Willpower)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T23:16:09-07:00","id":1448943,"title":"","content":"Define wyrm creatures. Alot of things PING on sense wyrm. Kitsune, People who eat Fast Food....anyone who's worked at the wrong place... This isn't D&amp;D and you didn't get detect Evil. Now are KJ litterally the Damned? Absolutely. The majority went to hell that they deserved to go to. Most of them wouldn't even question that. Do you accept their second chance or not is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T00:17:56-07:00","id":1448946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1448925#post1448925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Reference Note: By canon, wraiths only register to Sense Wyrm if the Shadow's Angst is greater than the Psyche's Willpower)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you ave a reference for that?<br /> <br /> While <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> is right about that a lot of things ping on sense wyrm and it isn't &quot;Detect Evil&quot; (like discussed elsewhere and detailed in the Storyteller's Handbook revised, iirc), there is the assumption that additional successes reveal more information on the taint and might allow discern a person feeling guilty after having killed in a war, from a person who witnessed a rape, to a person having eaten fast food, from a manager exploiting his colleagues, from a person planing a murder, from a person planning suicide....<br /> <br /> In any case, there is the question if any being is so corrupt, that it will always register as wyrm, without magical concealment. Fomori and banes come to mind first. BSD, too.<br /> As for Kuei-Jin I would assume that they are akin to Risen and Mummies and their Wyrm taint should be governed by their actions. In case that some stats represent this, like humanity does for vampires, than that is a good approximation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T00:33:57-07:00","id":1448948,"title":"","content":"I mean just pinging on sense wyrm doesn't mean much. You can be intrinsically tainted by locations/actions/etc Now my personal head canon on KIndred is that the reason some of them don't Ping to the wyrm is that its Aura advantage from their Path. Humanity's aura advantage is seeming like a normal person. Those who get aura advantage are in the right area where one doesn't sense wyrm by mechanics and leaves things open on other paths.as options.<br /> <br /> It makes it questionable whether wyrm taint is innate to the kindred condition or not.<br /> <br /> That being said all the trauma and wickedness of Hell probably scars the soul in ways that really can't be &quot;clensed&quot;. But whether taint is from being a victim or active servant is kind of a big issue in werewolf in general. I don't think there's really a seperate answer for KJ vs anything else. Are they servants of the wyrm? Some absolutely are. Some want to &quot;fix&quot; the wyrm back to its natural state. Some are just assholes who got theirs and don't care much about others..<br /> <br /> Its complicated, and this is before the occasional war between courts when some ancestor wants a new Dragonsnest.<br /> <br /> i","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T13:19:04-07:00","id":1449041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1448946#post1448946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you ave a reference for that?<br /> <br /> While <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> is right about that a lot of things ping on sense wyrm and it isn't &quot;Detect Evil&quot; (like discussed elsewhere and detailed in the Storyteller's Handbook revised, iirc), there is the assumption that additional successes reveal more information on the taint and might allow discern a person feeling guilty after having killed in a war, from a person who witnessed a rape, to a person having eaten fast food, from a manager exploiting his colleagues, from a person planing a murder, from a person planning suicide....<br /> <br /> In any case, there is the question if any being is so corrupt, that it will always register as wyrm, without magical concealment. Fomori and banes come to mind first. BSD, too.<br /> As for Kuei-Jin I would assume that they are akin to Risen and Mummies and their Wyrm taint should be governed by their actions. In case that some stats represent this, like humanity does for vampires, than that is a good approximation.</div> </div> </div> </div>W:tA Storyteller's Handbook Revised, page 200. My reference for Hungry Dead like Gui Ren registering as creatures of corruption comes from the crossover section of the KotE Companion, which hasn't been superceded in 23 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T19:21:12-07:00","id":1449077,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the Hunter's Talon fetish which doubles the damage vs Wyrm creatures, and whether it works on Kuei-Jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T21:35:04-07:00","id":1449086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449077#post1449077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the Hunter's Talon fetish which doubles the damage vs Wyrm creatures, and whether it works on Kuei-Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would you have it work on wyrm tainted but not BSD garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T22:29:26-07:00","id":1449092,"title":"","content":"Stargazer Revised Book says some have Wyrm-tainted marks some are not. I think very high dharma (7+ IIRC) will make you not wyrmish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T14:21:50-07:00","id":1449284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449086#post1449086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Would you have it work on wyrm tainted but not BSD garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't BSD considered Wyrm creatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T15:06:32-07:00","id":1449286,"title":"","content":"Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Before actually performing the BSD initiation rites, a BSD Cub is just heavily Wyrm tainted (and capable of being cleansed of that even if few Tribes would consider trying to adopt one). By actually dancing the Spiral, they become one with the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could see this as a bit of a retcon explanation to reconcile a few earlier things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T13:52:43-07:00","id":1449372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449286#post1449286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Before actually performing the BSD initiation rites, a BSD Cub is just heavily Wyrm tainted (and capable of being cleansed of that even if few Tribes would consider trying to adopt one). By actually dancing the Spiral, they become one with the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could see this as a bit of a retcon explanation to reconcile a few earlier things.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue, that a cub born of a (partly) BSD parentage isn't a BSD and not even necessarily tainted until exposed to events that generate taint. This would happen early on, if the child was exposed to BSD and their &quot;way of living&quot; (for lack of a better term)....<br /> <br /> There is however a short story in &quot;When will you Rage&quot; (iirc). Samuel Haight (yes, that guy) is selling information about the garou to some scientists (DNA, I assume) in exchange for a clone of himself (yes, much like Jango Fett got a little Boba for volunteering his DNA, Sammy got a little Mini-Me for selling out the garou). While waiting for the deal to conclude he becomes aware that his high school girlfriend's son is kidnapped. So, the WoD's most badass hunter (at this point he doesn't have most of his powers yet, I gather) investigates and realises, that his Ex is kinfolk, with a linage that might lead back to the white howlers and her son's father is a pure bred BSD, who until the child hit puberty lead a normal human life. No BSD connection or wyrm influence so far. Sammy of course goes after the BSD kidnappers and comes in conflict with garou from the Western Eye sept aswell.<br /> <br /> Once any garou who successfully passes the first level dancing the spiral becomes enlightened (or crazy) to the ways of the wyrm. But this isn't a level of corruption that is unredeemable. If one is willing to take a story there. It is a really really rare thing to happen, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T14:21:18-07:00","id":1449377,"title":"","content":"My simple answer: No. Most Wan Gui are not Wyrm creatures any more than most Kindred are. Akuma, Scorpion Eaters and others who actively serve the Yama Kings are, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T15:36:54-07:00","id":1449388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449284#post1449284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't BSD considered Wyrm creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are ways for Garou to gain the flaw wyrm taint without them actively dancing the spiral","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T22:42:58-07:00","id":1449423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449377#post1449377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My simple answer: No. Most Wan Gui are not Wyrm creatures any more than most Kindred are. Akuma, Scorpion Eaters and others who actively serve the Yama Kings are, however.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My complicated answer is very much sort of. Especially Kindred. But thus require the 3 tyoes of wyrm creature.<br /> <br /> 1. Those who are marked by the Wyrm, this has no moral component. Its like eating an evil sandwich. the Curse of caine is intrinsically ENTROPIC, its also Static. Being a Wriath is intrinsically Entropic these are just the way things are.<br /> <br /> 2. Those who's actions are toxic. When a corporation say puts profits over people it doesn't matter if they are actively in service to the wyrm or not the wyrm benefits. IN this scenario.. Most Kindred and KJ are in a society this exlicitly very toxic. I edge towards Kindred society being worse because there's no &quot;ends&quot; that I see as justifying the wyrminess of the camarilla/sabbat/etc They are all toxic they all hurt people and all the do is prevent monsters from getting their due. IN THEORY The various KJ sects promote one realizing one's second chance and thus is &quot;better&quot; but honestly their fail rate is pretty high and using good claims to justify monsterous acts has been pretty par for the course in human society<br /> <br /> 3. Finally there are Akuma, Infernalists, Followers of Set, Baali.This is not meant to be a complete list nor do I need to see a &quot;Not all... splat&quot;. Its a broad category of people who knowing actively engage in corruption for corruptions sake whether its for power, or to fight the aeons or what have you. They are in active service they know what they are doing has some sort of greater resonence. These ar the ones who most directly match what a Garou might think of as a servant of the wyrm. The difference between this category and category 2 is really the a difference between a Toxic waste dumping company and Pentex.<br /> <br /> 3a. Knowing followers of the wyrm. They are the minority of the minority because even KOTE isn't a game about Garou. but enough of them exist to I say comfortably give them theirown thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T23:53:34-07:00","id":1449429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449377#post1449377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My simple answer: No. Most Wan Gui are not Wyrm creatures any more than most Kindred are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sold on the &quot;most&quot; quantifier. While Humanity 7 carries the label &quot;normal&quot;, I think that a lot of vampires are at humanity 5 or 6, which would be &quot;removed&quot; and &quot;distant&quot;, respectively. Overall, the number of vampires that have taint on them might be larger than the number that hasn't (solely based on the humanity rating and not withstanding wyrm taint gained through recent actions).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T13:58:45-07:00","id":1449489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449429#post1449429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sold on the &quot;most&quot; quantifier. While Humanity 7 carries the label &quot;normal&quot;, I think that a lot of vampires are at humanity 5 or 6, which would be &quot;removed&quot; and &quot;distant&quot;, respectively. Overall, the number of vampires that have taint on them might be larger than the number that hasn't (solely based on the humanity rating and not withstanding wyrm taint gained through recent actions).</div> </div> </div> </div>And P'o is effectively Anti-Humanity, per Demon Hunter X. Since Gui Ren have that at a minimum of 3, they're kind of in the hole when it comes to this. It'd be like having a maximum Humanity of 7 or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T23:20:01-07:00","id":1449515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449429#post1449429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sold on the &quot;most&quot; quantifier. While Humanity 7 carries the label &quot;normal&quot;, I think that a lot of vampires are at humanity 5 or 6, which would be &quot;removed&quot; and &quot;distant&quot;, respectively. Overall, the number of vampires that have taint on them might be larger than the number that hasn't (solely based on the humanity rating and not withstanding wyrm taint gained through recent actions).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Road of Humanity's aura is to conceal the supernatural qualities. I am not sure I am sold on high humanity as making one non wyrm tainted vs covering it up. That being said those who can maintain high humanity are not likely actively making the wyrm stronger but I also don't imagine humanity 7+ is a long term solution in Kindred society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T12:59:17-07:00","id":1452040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1449377#post1449377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My simple answer: No. Most Wan Gui are not Wyrm creatures any more than most Kindred are. Akuma, Scorpion Eaters and others who actively serve the Yama Kings are, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends of the Yama King<br /> Take Haha no Fukami for example; Haha No Fukami, translated as Mother of the Depths, is one of the Yama Kings who holds the title of &quot;Empress of Pearls&quot;, ruling over the Hell of Seven Burning Seas. Although not one of the original Yama Kings, Haha no Fukami was the primal ocean mother during the First Age, but changed to her current duty at the request of the August Personage of Jade. Perhaps the least corrupt of the Yama Kings, she is the punisher of crimes made against or upon the ocean, as well as evil acts involving the abuse of fire or water. <br /> A Kuei-jin in the service of her would be detected by sense Wyrm? Personally I don't think so<br /> Same goes for Tou Shen, ruler of the Feverish Hell, who presiding over those who profited from smallpox or even for the servants of Emma-O, the Lord of Kakuri, the Night Realm<br /> To be honest, I think if Tou Mu wouldn't hate the Kuei-jin with hot burning passion to the point she refuses to accept them as Akuma,her servants wouldn't ping the radar either<br /> <br /> As for the rest of them, it depends of the Dharma and Chi<br /> A Trashing Dragon would confuse the hell out of a wandering garou or any shapeshifter really... while the Cranes are more weaverish, with their love and detication to law and order for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T14:05:37-07:00","id":1452058,"title":"","content":"I thought the Yama Kings were all inherently evil, to the point that you were discouraged from playing their servants the same way you would be from playing an Infernalist in a Western campaign (the one line you\u2019re not supposed to cross)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T17:25:10-07:00","id":1452095,"title":"","content":"I side with those who think the Garou would sense and attack the Kuei Jin on sight. Even the Beast Courts consider the Wan Kuei vile, keeping encounters rare and just cordial enough to keep the peace around nodes and caerns, and misdirecting their Rage in fits of conveniently religious prejudice is pretty much the western Garou's trademark through much of their history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T21:34:47-07:00","id":1453011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1452058#post1452058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Yama Kings were all inherently evil, to the point that you were discouraged from playing their servants the same way you would be from playing an Infernalist in a Western campaign (the one line you\u2019re not supposed to cross)</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority of the Yama Kings are corrupt and have turned their backs on their duty in the name of power, but there's still a few who haven't done so. Notably though those Yama Kings generally don't make Akuma or corrupt others into their services like the evil ones do, so you wouldn't be able to play an Akuma to one of them anyway. <br /> <br /> As to the primary question, Kuei-jin should generally trigger Sense Wyrm. Some Dharmas might trigger it less, especially as the Wan Kuei reaches higher levels (for example higher dharma Resplendent Cranes or Rising Phoenixes would likely not trigger Sense Wyrm in the same way high Humanity vampires don't). On the other hand, some dharmas should always trigger Sense Wyrm, like the Devil Tigers or Song of Shadows. In fact, truly high ranking Devil Tigers would probably come off as incredibly powerful and corrupt Wyrm creatures to the point where a Rank 10 Devil Tiger would probably be comparable in corruption as a Maeljin Incarna. <br /> <br /> That said, the Emerald Courts have a tradition of engaging in diplomacy with the Wan Kuei, and there is a recognition they they have a role to play, even Devil Tigers, so shapeshifters would be <i>slightly</i> less trigger happy than western werewolves when it comes to immediately murdering wyrm-smelling creatures. But if a Wan Keui shows up unnanounced at a Caern, or gets found hurting kinfolk or if the shapeshifter is just having a slightly bad day, then goodbye Wan Kuei. And especially for younger Wan Kuei, there's not going to be any real fallout or retribution from that. Ultimately the Wan Kuei would probably be recommended to walk on eggshells around shapeshifters, and open warfare and conflict between the two groups is extremely common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T16:15:36-07:00","id":1453212,"title":"","content":"I think the Garou would view them as Wyrm creatures and also find the Kuei-Jin's whole description of themselves as heroic undead fighting demons to be lunacy.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Stargazers would probably know them better but still view their &quot;noble demon&quot; sticke silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T19:28:11-07:00","id":1453226,"title":"","content":"At least in Asia, spirits, the Mokole, etc all remember how the Wan Kuei used to be the Wan Xian before they fell from grace and were punished for their crimes. They wouldn't view them as heroic, but then even the Wan Kuei don't view themselves as heroes, they consider themselves former criminals trying to atone for their prior failings by properly performing their proper heavenly-ordained role (which is pretty much anything but being a hero).<br /> <br /> Of course Garou outside of Asia have probably never heard of the Wan Xian and don't have the sort of relationship with Mokole or Asian spirits to remember that, so to them Wan Kuei are just another type of bloodsucking monster, albeit one more dangerous than regular bloodsuckers because they can enter the Umbra and somewhat move around during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T21:19:44-07:00","id":1533442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Busboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1448916#post1448916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say not inherently---in fact inherently they're creatures of &quot;balance&quot; and potentially somewhat resistant (having both Lifesight and Deathsight, they can shift between lower and middle umbral energies; they're not just undead revenants but creatures of both flesh and spirit, somewhat like Garou). However, those of the Scorpion Eater Dharma, and those who have outright become Akuma, are extremely of-the-Wyrm. From a WTA perspective I'd translate the Yama Kings as essentially corrupted Incarnae of some sort or other.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448909-are-kuei-jin-wyrm-creatures?p=1448918#post1448918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it depends on their current chi balance. Balanced and yang imbalanced don't ping as Wyrm. Ying imbalance (because of the death energy), high level of demon chi, and having tainted chi, should all ping as having Wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> They most certainly aren't inherently creatures of the Wyrm, so things like Rite of Cleansing wouldn't just cause them pain. Though letting it manipulate chi levels is probably a bit much for a level 1 Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thread necromancy, but I found a quote that I think clarifies the issue a bit more, bold is mine:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20 Changing Breeds p.35</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">n the Middle Kingdom, the traditional protectorate<br /> of the Beast Courts, <b>Wyrm-tainted creatures called the<br /> Kuei-Jin</b> tricked the Changing Breeds into what is now<br /> referred to as the War of Shame.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So as far as official material is concerned Kuei-Jin are in fact, Wyrm innately tainted. So if I am reading how that works correctly: the Rite of Cleansing should hurt them, the Hunter\u2019s Talons fetish would do double damage, and Sense Wyrm should detect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T21:31:49-07:00","id":1533444,"title":"","content":"That's hardly a definitely citation? The books call western vampires Wyrm-tainted all the time, but it's not a mechanical truth. It's an assumption many Garou have, but in truth only most are.<br /> <br /> Lots of the Wan Kuei are going to ping as Wyrm-tainted because lots are going to be imbalanced towards Yin, their P'o, or having tainted Chi in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T23:46:23-07:00","id":1533446,"title":"","content":"There isn't really a definitive citation beyond that same part of the KotE companion I mentioned upthread (about 20 posts and 3 years ago), and also that they generally default to Vampire when some other bit of mechanics doesn't say otherwise.<br /> <br /> Until you progress far along a Dharma, you're a creature of hell. Even if you do progress far along some Dharma, it just makes you even more of one (Devil Tigers and Scorpion Eaters). The closest thing to Humanity, beyond the abandoned system used by the Kanbujian, is probably the Flame of the Rising Phoenix, and even that has some alien touches to it that make it not quite like Humanity. We're not really told how the other Dharmas register, but it's probably lower key than the others. <br /> <br /> (Whenever I read about the Rising Phoenixes, I keep thinking about Gintama episode 282, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zIv4DKKHfWc\" target=\"_blank\">the best vintage of filler there is</a>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}